# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A define parameter list ends at the first closing paren"

# The two definition rules declare their parameter lists differently, and the difference decides
# where the body starts.
#
#   macrodef.js    \\define\s+([^(\s]+)\(\s*([^)]*)\)          the list ends at the FIRST )
#   fnprocdef.js   \\(function|procedure|widget)\s+([^(\s]+)\((\s*([^)]*(?:\)\)[^)]*)*))?\)
#                                                              the list may carry )) pairs
#
# So a multi-valued-variable default, a:((var)), holds in a procedure, function or widget and
# does NOT hold in a define. Measured on TiddlyWiki's own parser:
#
#   \procedure p(a:((var))) body    param a, defaultType multivalue-variable, body "body"
#   \define    d(a:((var))) body    param a, default "((var",                 body ")) body"
#
# The define takes two literal parens into its default string and the body starts four characters
# earlier than the doubled form suggests. Painting an mvv default there invents a construct
# TiddlyWiki does not build, and moves the body with it.
#
# No parse-tree check can see this: a definition is stored rather than parsed, so the parser holds
# no opinion about any span inside it.

! A procedure takes a multi-valued-variable default

\procedure p.mvv(a:((var))) body
#                  ^^ punctuation.definition.mvv.default.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                    ^^^ variable.name.mvv.default.tiddlywiki5
#                       ^^ punctuation.definition.mvv.default.end.tiddlywiki5
#                         ^ punctuation.definition.variable.pragma.parameters.end.tiddlywiki5
#                           ^^^^ meta.variable.procedure.body.tiddlywiki5

! A define does not, and its body starts at the first closing paren

\define d.mvv(a:((var))) body
#               ^^ - punctuation.definition.mvv.default.begin.tiddlywiki5
#                    ^ punctuation.definition.variable.pragma.parameters.end.tiddlywiki5
#                     ^^ meta.variable.macro.body.tiddlywiki5
#                        ^^^^ meta.variable.macro.body.tiddlywiki5
